@* Batch VC-1 (R3): "ONE generic composition host ... renders any
   Arrangement ... mounting members via the ViewRegistry." Scope, disclosed:
   this component mounts a HOST's own GUEST -- the host slot itself stays
   each route page's own pre-existing markup (Reader.razor/Sources.razor's
   own content, unchanged shape), embedded at the exact point the OLD
   hardcoded `<World .../>` tag (Reader) used to sit. This is a deliberate,
   disclosed design choice, not a partial implementation of R3: SplitDivider
   itself is ALREADY a shared, reusable component whose own header comment
   (M-D3/B2, pre-VC-1) explicitly anticipates "a future second split host
   inherits the identical mechanic for free" -- i.e. each capable-of-hosting
   view owns its OWN divider wiring/width state, and this component's job is
   the GENERIC, registry-driven part: given the CURRENT ViewArrangement and
   "which view is asking," resolve who the guest is, mount it by NAME (never
   a hardcoded type), and wire the ownership-close/query-routing plumbing.
   The alternative (this component owning ONE outer flex div spanning both
   panes for every possible host) was investigated and rejected: Reader's
   own shift-tracking keydown/keyup wrapper (OnPageKeyDown/OnPageKeyUp, the
   ExplorerPopover bubble-catch mechanism) needs a shared DOM ancestor of
   [reader-page][its own popover] that predates this batch and is reader-
   specific -- forcing it up into a generic host risked a real, disclosed
   accessibility/keyboard regression for a purely structural win. See the
   batch report's own design section for the fuller trade discussion.

   R6 (arrangement-vocabulary conformance): EVERY LayoutKind this atom's own
   vocabulary can hold is a real branch below, including the unrecognized
   case -- fails LOUD (a visible toast, data-testid="composition-error"),
   never silently renders nothing, per the compiled ICompositionLayout
   contract's own Kind member. *@
@using BibleAtlas.Client.Contracts
@using BibleAtlas.Client.State
@using BibleAtlas.Client.Views
@inject StateAtom<ViewArrangement> ViewArrangementAtom
@inject ViewRegistry Registry

@{
    var arrangement = ViewArrangementAtom.Value;
}
@if (IsMyGuestSlot(arrangement))
{
    var guestName = arrangement.Members[1];
    var ctx = new ViewMountContext(
        SplitMode: true,
        IsHost: false,
        OnRequestClose: EventCallback.Factory.Create(this, () => ViewArrangementAtom.Dispatch(new CloseGuest())),
        RegisterQueryHandler: handler => _guestQueryHandler = handler);
    @Registry.Get(guestName).Mount(ctx)
}
else if (!LayoutKinds.IsKnown(arrangement.LayoutKind))
{
    <div class="toast" data-testid="composition-error">
        <p class="toast-message">Unrecognized arrangement layout "@arrangement.LayoutKind" -- ICompositionLayout.Kind is out of vocabulary.</p>
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>Which registered view is asking "who is my guest, if any" --
    /// e.g. Reader.razor passes <c>ViewNames.Reader</c>. Required: a
    /// composition host with no owner identity cannot tell a genuine "I am
    /// currently hosting" state from "some OTHER view is hosting, I have
    /// nothing to render" -- see <see cref="IsMyGuestSlot"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string HostName { get; set; } = null!;

    private Func<string, Task>? _guestQueryHandler;

    /// <summary>The composed "route a popover-originated scene query into my
    /// currently-mounted guest" delegate -- null while no split-h guest is
    /// mounted, or while the mounted guest never called
    /// <see cref="ViewMountContext.RegisterQueryHandler"/> (i.e. it doesn't
    /// support being a query-routing target at all, e.g. Sources). The host
    /// page reads this via <c>@ref</c> (see Reader.razor's own
    /// <c>_compositionHost</c> field) and forwards it to its OWN popover's
    /// <c>OnNavigateWorldInSplit</c> parameter -- the generalized "no
    /// nested-popup rule" (Batch H), unchanged behavior for reader+world,
    /// generically available to any future query-routable guest.</summary>
    public Func<string, Task> NavigateGuestInSplit => query => _guestQueryHandler?.Invoke(query) ?? Task.CompletedTask;

    private bool IsMyGuestSlot(ViewArrangement arrangement) =>
        arrangement.LayoutKind == LayoutKinds.SplitH && arrangement.Members.Count == 2 && arrangement.Members[0] == HostName;
}
